{"applicationId":"volfee","applicationRevision":"1","builder":{"contact":"https://github.com/ToanPham247","githubLogin":"ToanPham247","githubUserId":"173402366"},"contract":{"id":"public-pr-application-v3","submissionStandard":"2.0.0","validatorProfile":"intent-open-world-v1","version":"3.1.0"},"declarations":{"historicalEvidencePreserved":true,"noApprovalClaim":true,"noInheritedApproval":true,"noSecretsDeclared":true,"noUniswapEndorsementClaim":true,"publicInformationAcknowledged":true},"fidelity":{"reasonCode":null,"requirementBindings":[],"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","status":"unassessed"},"intentCapture":{"agentInterpretationStatus":"unconfirmed","captureStatus":"captured-verbatim-public-safe","facts":[{"confirmationStatus":"unconfirmed","id":"builder-public-idea","provenance":"owner-stated","sourceReferences":["original-idea"],"statement":"VolFee — a Uniswap v4 hook.\n\nOne v4 hook on a canonical dynamic-fee pool: the LP fee auto-calibrates to the pool's OWN realized volatility (an EWMA of the per-swap tick delta, no external price source or keeper) so LPs are paid more in volatile markets and traders less in calm ones; the hook also enforces the mandatory Programmable volume fee (10 bps platform owner liability plus the project remainder as a project-claimable liability) non-bypassably on the same pool.\n\nUser outcome: A creator launches a WETH-paired token in one canonical v4 pool whose LP fee reprices itself every swap from realized volatility, so passive LPs are paid the most exactly when toxic flow is worst and traders pay the least in calm markets, with no external price source, admin, keeper or upgrade.\n\nWhy v4: Only a v4 hook can (a) return a per-swap LP fee override (OVERRIDE_FEE_FLAG) in beforeSwap computed from the pool's own realized-volatility state, so the dynamic LP fee is set atomically per swap with no external price source or keeper, and (b) collect the mandatory volume fee non-bypassably through quadrant-dependent beforeSwap/afterSwap return deltas on the quote side of every canonical-pool swap. The volatility state is read in beforeSwap (before the swap) and updated in afterSwap (after it) so a swap can never lower its own fee.\n\n"}],"ideaSourcePath":"submission-v2/idea-source.v1.json","ideaSourceRepositoryRef":"primary","ideaSourceSha256":"sha256:d2b5e194e5ee605d6ee573f0913ef04d16e41ec3b003136610687dc8ce1ead84","language":"und","originalIdeaDisplayExcerpt":"VolFee — a Uniswap v4 hook.\n\nOne v4 hook on a canonical dynamic-fee pool: the LP fee auto-calibrates to the pool's OWN realized volatility (an EWMA of the per-swap tick delta, no external price source or keeper) so LPs are paid more in volatile markets and traders less in calm ones; the hook also enforces the mandatory Programmable volume fee (10 bps platform owner liability plus the project remainder as a project-claimable liability) non-bypassably on the same pool.\n\nUser outcome: A creator launches a WETH-paired token in one canonical v4 pool whose LP fee reprices itself every swap from realized volatility, so passive LPs are paid the most exactly when toxic flow is worst and traders pay the least in calm markets, with no external price source, admin, keeper or upgrade.\n\nWhy v4: Only a v4 hook can (a) return a per-swap LP fee override (OVERRIDE_FEE_FLAG) in beforeSwap computed from the pool's own realized-volatility state, so the dynamic LP fee is set atomically per swap with no external price source or keeper, and (b) collect the mandatory volume fee non-bypassably through quadrant-dependent beforeSwap/afterSwap return deltas on the quote side of every canonical-pool swap. The volatility state is read in beforeSwap (before the swap) and updated in afterSwap (after it) so a swap can never lower its own fee.\n\n","schemaVersion":"1.0.0","unresolvedMaterialDecisions":["The builder idea is captured, but its architecture has not been interpreted or confirmed yet."]},"lineage":{"kind":"new","previous":null},"policyBindings":{"feeApplicability":"n